CHUNK({"chunk":"U","module":"m5","topics":[{"id":"m5-env-monitoring","title":"Environmental health monitoring","short":"Env health monitoring","blurb":"What environmental health monitoring is, its five key aspects, the factors it watches, how it works, remote sensing and environmental databases such as ENVIS.","source":"Lecture W5 (AI and IoT in Environmental Monitoring), pages 1–2, 7","tabs":[{"title":"Definition","html":"\n          <p class=\"lead\"><b>Environmental health monitoring</b>: systematic collection, analysis, assessment of environmental data (air, water, soil) to <b>detect changes, identify health risks, predict future conditions</b> affecting public health.</p>\n          <p>Does: current state, trends, informs authorities, supports policy, checks management tools.</p>\n          <table class=\"tbl\">\n            <tbody>\n              <tr><td><b>Data collection</b></td><td>Regular exposure and health data from air, water, soil and more</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>Risk assessment</b></td><td>Risks that conditions pose to public health</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>Trend analysis</b></td><td>Changes over time; predict future scenarios</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>Policy and decisions</b></td><td>Information for policymakers, health authorities, public</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>Public health protection</b></td><td>The ultimate goal: find problems and act</td></tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n        "},{"title":"What and how","html":"\n          <p><b>Factors monitored</b>:</p>\n          <ul>\n            <li><b>Air</b>: pollutants and aerosols, mainly in cities.</li>\n            <li><b>Water</b>: temperature, acidity, pollutants in rivers etc.</li>\n            <li><b>Soil and waste</b>: soil state; waste management preventing contamination.</li>\n            <li><b>Biodiversity</b>: changes in natural resources.</li>\n          </ul>\n          <p><b>Methods</b>: ground sampling, <b>satellite observation</b>, <b>environmental modelling</b>. Feed reports, government, international talks.</p>\n        "},{"title":"Remote sensing, databases","html":"\n          <ul>\n            <li><b>Remote sensing</b>: info about an object <b>without touching it</b>; agriculture, forestry, land cover, water resources.</li>\n            <li><b>Database</b>: collection of inter-related data. Examples:\n              <ul>\n                <li>The Ministry of Environment and Forests.</li>\n                <li><b>NMIS</b> (National Management Information System): R&amp;D projects and the scientists and staff involved.</li>\n                <li><b>ENVIS</b> (Environmental Information System): a network of databases across India.</li>\n              </ul>\n            </li>\n          </ul>\n          <div class=\"note heads-up\">Course text says ENVIS works in \"25 countries all over the country\": means about 25 centres within India.</div>\n        "}],"flashcards":[{"front":"Define environmental health monitoring.","back":"Systematic collection and analysis of environmental data to detect changes, identify health risks and predict conditions affecting public health."},{"front":"Five key aspects of environmental health monitoring?","back":"Data collection, risk assessment, trend analysis, policy and decisions, public health protection."},{"front":"Three monitoring methods?","back":"Ground sampling, satellite observation, environmental modelling."}],"cardCount":6,"formulaCount":0},{"id":"m5-ai-monitoring","title":"Role of AI in environmental monitoring","short":"AI in monitoring","blurb":"AI for prediction, conservation and hazards, the software tools from LSTM forecasting to digital twins and e-noses, and two case studies.","source":"Lecture W5 (AI and IoT in Environmental Monitoring), pages 2–3, 5–7","tabs":[{"title":"Uses","html":"\n          <p class=\"lead\">AI analyses huge sensor and satellite datasets to <b>predict, detect and track</b> pollution, deforestation and other change in real time.</p>\n          <table class=\"tbl\">\n            <tbody>\n              <tr><td><b>Monitoring and prediction</b></td><td>Air: forecast pollution, find sources (low-cost sensors, satellites). Water: real-time contaminant alerts, trigger filtration. Climate: CO₂, glacier mass, sea level. <b>Flood prediction</b>: early warnings, evacuation</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>Conservation</b></td><td><b>Habitat mapping</b> (deep learning on satellite/aerial images). <b>Wildlife monitoring</b> (camera traps, GPS, acoustic). <b>Anomalies</b>: poaching, illegal logging, unusual boat movements</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>Hazards</b></td><td>Sensors and <b>edge AI</b> detect hazardous substances; early warning systems</td></tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n        "},{"title":"AI tools","html":"\n          <table class=\"tbl\">\n            <tbody>\n              <tr><td><b>Geospatial analysis</b></td><td>AI on satellite and drone images (e.g. FlyPix AI): deforestation, illegal dumping, land use</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>Predictive analytics</b></td><td>ML forecasts floods, weather, pollution; <b>LSTM</b> (Long Short-Term Memory) predicts air quality from past data</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>Robotics</b></td><td>Robots monitor hazardous air, clean polluted water surfaces</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>Digital twin</b></td><td><b>Virtual replica</b> of a real system (e.g. water treatment plant) for simulation, optimisation</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>E-nose</b></td><td>Electronic nose: identifies hazardous gases by chemical signature; industrial leak watch</td></tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n          <p>AI + <b>IoT devices and sensors</b> = real-time data and alerts; ML turns satellite, sensor, drone data into insights.</p>\n        "},{"title":"Case studies","html":"\n          <div class=\"vs\">\n            <div class=\"side\"><h4>IIT Kharagpur: arsenic</h4><p><b>Problem</b>: arsenic in Eastern India groundwater. <b>Solution</b>: AI on geoscience data maps high/low arsenic zones in the <b>Ganga delta</b>, quantifies exposure. <b>Impact</b>: safe drinking water sources.</p></div>\n            <div class=\"side\"><h4>The Ocean Cleanup: plastic</h4><p><b>Problem</b>: ocean plastic harms marine life. <b>Solution</b>: AI detects debris, maps litter in remote ocean. <b>Impact</b>: targeted, efficient clean-up.</p></div>\n          </div>\n        "}],"flashcards":[{"front":"Three ways AI helps conservation?","back":"Habitat mapping, wildlife monitoring, detecting illegal activity."},{"front":"Which AI model can forecast air quality from past data?","back":"<b>LSTM</b> (Long Short-Term Memory)."},{"front":"What is a digital twin?","back":"A <b>virtual replica</b> of a physical system used to simulate and optimise it."}],"cardCount":6,"formulaCount":0},{"id":"m5-iot-monitoring","title":"Role of IoT in environmental monitoring","short":"IoT in monitoring","blurb":"How connected sensors help, the eight benefits, the five sensor types, and integrated platforms such as dashboards, ISO 14001 EMS and smart waste systems.","source":"Lecture W5 (AI and IoT in Environmental Monitoring), pages 3–6","tabs":[{"title":"Benefits","html":"\n          <p class=\"lead\"><b>IoT</b>: connected sensors send real-time air/water quality, temperature, humidity data for analysis, remote monitoring, predictive alerts.</p>\n          <ol>\n            <li><b>Real-time data</b> on pollutants, water purity, temperature, humidity.</li>\n            <li><b>Remote monitoring</b> of hard-to-reach places without people.</li>\n            <li><b>Predictive analysis</b> when combined with machine learning.</li>\n            <li><b>Automated responses</b>: switch on air purifiers or water treatment above thresholds.</li>\n            <li><b>Resource management</b>: soil moisture sensors optimise irrigation; wildlife tracking.</li>\n            <li><b>Public awareness</b> through shared live data.</li>\n            <li><b>Lower costs</b>: fewer site visits.</li>\n            <li><b>Pollutant detection</b>: subtle changes like toxic gases.</li>\n          </ol>\n        "},{"title":"Sensors","html":"\n          <table class=\"tbl\">\n            <thead><tr><th>Sensor</th><th>Measures</th></tr></thead>\n            <tbody>\n              <tr><td><b>Air quality</b></td><td>PM2.5, PM10, CO, SO₂, NOₓ; finds hotspots, health warnings</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>Water quality</b></td><td>pH, <b>dissolved oxygen</b>, turbidity, chemical contaminants; early effluent detection</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>Soil</b></td><td>Moisture, temperature, pH, nutrients (<b>NPK</b>), contamination; food safety, sustainable farming</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>Acoustic</b></td><td>Forest soundscapes: wildlife, <b>illegal logging, poaching</b></td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>Wearable</b></td><td>A person's own exposure to pollutants in real time</td></tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n        "},{"title":"Platforms","html":"\n          <ul>\n            <li><b>Cloud EHS platforms</b> (e.g. EHS Insight, Envirosuite): environmental, health, safety data; analytics, compliance.</li>\n            <li><b>Real-time dashboards</b>: live sensor visuals; trends, instant anomaly alerts, maps.</li>\n            <li><b>Environmental Management Systems</b> (<b>ISO 14001</b>): IoT data + AI cut company impact.</li>\n            <li><b>Smart waste management</b>: bin fill-level sensors, optimised routes; less overflow, fewer truck emissions.</li>\n          </ul>\n          <div class=\"note exam\">AI and IoT work together: <b>IoT collects</b> the data, <b>AI analyses</b> it and predicts.</div>\n        "}],"flashcards":[{"front":"What does IoT add to monitoring?","back":"Connected sensors giving <b>real-time, remote</b> data and alerts."},{"front":"Example of an IoT automated response?","back":"Switching on air purifiers or water treatment when pollution passes a threshold."},{"front":"What do soil sensors measure?","back":"Moisture, temperature, pH, <b>NPK</b> nutrients."}],"cardCount":6,"formulaCount":0}],"figures":[]});
